  "category": "Uncategorized",
  "description": "**Fix html5-qrcode Scanning & Audio Feedback on Firefox Mobile**\n\nhtml5-qrcode library fails on Firefox for Android in two ways: camera/scan initiation doesn't work, and success audio (beep) doesn't play after scan.\n\n**Requirements:**\n- Debug Firefox Mobile-specific camera access (`getUserMedia` quirks, permission flow, constraints). Firefox may require different adapter/fallback or manifest entries\n- Fix audio playback for scan success event — root cause is likely Firefox autoplay policy blocking play(). Use Web Audio API `AudioContext.resume()` after user gesture\n- Test on physical Firefox Android device (GeckoView), not desktop emulation\n- No regression on Chrome/Safari mobile\n\n**Fallback mechanisms:**\n- If audio blocked: use Vibration API (`navigator.vibrate()`) as tactile feedback\n- If audio blocked: visual flash/indicator on screen as fallback\n- Multiple rapid scans must queue/cancel audio properly\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- Firefox Private Browsing mode (stricter permissions)\n- Firefox Focus (minimal browser, no persistent storage, different API surface)\n- Firefox with strict Enhanced Tracking Protection (may block media APIs)\n- Device in silent/vibrate mode\n- Low-power / battery saver mode affecting media APIs\n- Tab backgrounding or screen lock during scan\n- Camera permission denied → graceful error message (not silent hang)\n- Rear vs front camera initialization parity\n- html5-qrcode library version compat with Firefox WebRTC implementation (GeckoView vs legacy)\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- Existing feature branch `feature-1781796894404-1fya40cv8ss` (modify in-place vs new fix feature)",
